  "summary": "Fixes node and wallet targeting bugs in two functional wallet tests. In wallet_keypool_topup.py, it ensures backup and restore operations target each node's respective wallet rather than mistakenly reusing node1's files across all output types. In wallet_createwallet.py, it corrects an assertion to test the newly created avoid_reuse wallet rather than re-checking the previous wallet handle.",
  "problem": "Test coverage for keypool restoration across p2sh-segwit, bech32, and bech32m wallets was ineffective because nodes 2 through 4 were restarted using their original wallets instead of restored backups, causing tests to pass trivially without actually exercising restore functionality. Additionally, encryption verification for wallets created with avoid_reuse in wallet_createwallet.py was bypassed due to checking the wrong variable handle.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'Adding just that assertion on master makes the test fail at node2.'",
    "Commit 215f8b828b: 'The p2sh-segwit, bech32 and bech32m checks therefore passed trivially: that wallet had derived the keys and received the funds itself.'",
    "Commit 13b2d21beb: 'Since c5d3787367 the avoid_reuse section of wallet_createwallet calls w7.walletpassphrase, repeating the assertion made on w7 just before it, so the w8 wallet it creates was never checked for encryption.'"
